course: dictionary
lesson: 15701
title: Tons: a lot, or a weight
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word tons can mean a lot. When you hear «I've got tons of homework», you do not count every sheet. Tons of means a great amount, and the words around it show that it is about quantity, not weight.
explain: Tons can also mean weight. A ton is a unit for heavy things, like lorries, ships and whales. «The lorry carried five tons of sand» is about how heavy the sand is, because lorries carry heavy loads.
explain: Ask yourself: is this about how heavy something is, or how much of something there is? Then try your meaning in the sentence. If «tons of fun» still makes sense as "a lot of fun", you have chosen the right meaning.
fact: Tons is the plural of ton, a unit of weight.
fact: «Tons of» is informal and means a lot, or a great amount: «There were tons of people at the match.»
fact: A ton in the USA is 2,000 pounds, about 907 kg. An old UK (long) ton is 2,240 pounds, about 1,016 kg.
fact: A metric ton, usually spelled tonne, is 1,000 kilograms.
fact: In UK slang, «doing a ton» means 100 miles per hour, and in cricket a ton is 100 runs.
exercise: «I've got tons of homework tonight.» What does tons of mean here? | A small heap | *A great amount | Two sheets of paper | A weight of exactly one kilo
exercise: «The lorry carried five tons of sand.» What are tons measuring here? | Length | Time | Colour | *Weight
exercise: What does tons mean in «She's tons better at chess than me»? | *Much, by a great amount | Weighing five kilos | Not at all | Only just
test: A metric ton is the same as how many kilograms? | 500 | *1,000 | 100 | 2,240
test: In cricket, a ton means how many runs? | 50 | *100 | 10 | 2,000
exam: Safety signs on a bridge show a limit of 20 t. What does the t stand for? | *tonnes, a unit of weight | tea | time | tiles
